# `UNDELIVERED-MESSAGE-MARKING`/`SEQUENCE-TIME-GAP`/`SEQUENCE-PARTICIPANT-GROUPING`: the three constructs this genre REFUSED. None
# of them is a withdrawal — the genre never declared any of the three — so
# each gets its own diagnostic shape: the ground the ruling gave, and the
# spelling that works instead.
#
# `gap` is the interesting one mechanically. It is BOTH `timing`'s child
# keyword and the word this genre refused, so the refusal has to be consulted
# BEFORE the typed-block-child exemption or the author is told "gap is a
# typed-block child", which is true of the language and says nothing about the
# ruling they have run into.
#
# `lost=` is the other interesting one: it is NOT in the language's option
# registry at all, because refusing it means adding no key. So its named
# diagnostic fires on the UNKNOWN-OPTION path rather than on the
# inapplicable-key path — which is how a refusal can be named without the
# spelling being registered.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
lifeline s "S"
group participants "Both ends"
gap "T1 fires"
message c -> s "never arrives" lost="the issuing server does not answer"
